{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2580 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7e3ee612cfb3011547dfb276d4f2c85441ec4a234586c6edfc196a4abb35051a" :edb/db-before-t 2579 :edb/db-after-t 2580 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535892 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:04:31.606Z" 13194139535892 true] [17592186119673 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372993 13194139535892 true] [17592186119673 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373007 13194139535892 true] [17592186119673 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373014 13194139535892 true] [17592186119674 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373000 13194139535892 true] [17592186119674 1020 #edb/ref 17592186373021 13194139535892 true] [17592186372993 1017 #edb/ref 17592186372994 13194139535892 true] [17592186372993 1089 "q-131225" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372993 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535892 true] [17592186372993 1100 "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372993 1113 #uuid "f000c9ed-a6ae-5faa-9857-7ca6186fd3c0" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372993 1145 "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{tan}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372995 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372996 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372997 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372998 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372999 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1041 "selection" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372999 13194139535892 true] [17592186372994 1110 #uuid "0cf77a15-fd72-5c6d-b784-4190e8d603e2" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372995 1034 "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535892 true] [17592186372995 1111 #uuid "d3f48bee-4c65-5fac-bfd3-3466028bd795" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372996 1034 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535892 true] [17592186372996 1111 #uuid "aaec0542-9350-526b-93e8-70e97358b248" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372997 1034 "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535892 true] [17592186372997 1111 #uuid "a5b39a93-ff50-51b1-8c31-9beabf4ce7c0" 13194139535892 true] [17592186372998 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" 13194139535892 true] [1759